1. What is an EC2 Instance?
EC2 = Elastic Compute Cloud
Amazon EC2 provides virtual servers in AWS that you can use to run applications.

2.EC2 AMI
An AMI is a template used to create an EC2 instance
AMI is a template containing the operating system and required configuration used to launch EC2 instances.

EC2 Instance Type
Instance type determines the CPU, memory, networking, and other capabilities of your EC2 instance.
t3.micro
t3.small
t3.medium
t3.large
m7i.large
c7i.large
R7i.large

6. Key Pair
A key pair is used to securely connect to an EC2 instance.

7. VPC
EC2 instances run inside a VPC.
VPC = Virtual Private Cloud
Think of it as your private network in AWS.

8. Subnet
A subnet is a smaller network inside a VPC.

9. Public vs Private EC2
Public EC2
An EC2 instance can have public connectivity.
Private EC2
No direct inbound access from the internet.

10. Security Group
Security Group acts as a virtual firewall for EC2.

11. EBS
EBS = Elastic Block Store
EBS provides persistent block storage for EC2.

13. Elastic IP
An Elastic IP is a static public IPv4 address associated with an AWS resource such as an EC2 instance.

14. IAM Role
Instead of putting AWS access keys inside an EC2 server, we can attach an IAM Role.

15. User Data
EC2 User Data allows you to execute commands/scripts during instance initialization.

“EC2 is AWS's virtual server service. When launching an EC2 instance, I select an AMI, instance type, VPC/subnet, security group, storage, and authentication method. In production, I would normally use IAM roles, private subnets, an ALB, Auto Scaling Groups, CloudWatch monitoring, and multiple Availability Zones for security, scalability, and high availability.”





